  "steps": [
   "Heat the oven to 190°C (170°C fan). Halve the peaches, pull out the stones and slice them. Toss in a medium baking dish with the raspberries, cornflour and half the cinnamon.",
   "In a mixing bowl, stir together the flour, oats, sugar, hazelnuts, the rest of the cinnamon and the salt.",
   "Pour in the oil and rub it through with your fingertips until the mixture clumps into rough crumbs.",
   "Scatter the crumble evenly over the fruit without pressing it down.",
   "Bake for 30 to 35 minutes, until the top is golden and crisp and the fruit is bubbling up at the edges.",
   "Leave to cool for 10 minutes so the juices thicken, then spoon into bowls. It is good warm or cold, and leftovers keep in the fridge for 2 days."
